WEBVTT

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:29.380
It's pretty crowded.

00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:33.720
Tsumugi, the ocean's really pretty!

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.880
Come on out.

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:42.390
Carry me...

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:47.650
You're a big girl now, so you 
can get out on your own, right?

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:52.150
I'm a kitty right now.

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:54.470
So I can't do it by myself.

00:00:55.270 --> 00:00:56.440
I see.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:00.780
If you're a kitty, maybe you can't.

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:15.440
Tsumugi, look.

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:17.510
Doesn't that look fun?

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:21.340
I brought your swimsuit, in case 
you want to go in the water.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:22.970
No...

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:26.750
Okay, let's go for a walk.

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:28.730
There's a beach clubhouse over there.

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:29.750
Let's go!

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:31.980
<b>Beach Clubhouse</b>

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:06.450
<b>Summer Vacation, Kitty, and Aji</b>

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:31.030
Geh?

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:32.600
Today

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:32.600
Tokyo Musashino-shi
Clear
Chance of Rain: 0%
Humidity: 34%
Wind Speed: 1 m/s

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:32.600
35 degrees?

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:35.160
Kotori...

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:37.930
Let's turn on the air conditioner...

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:42.360
We said we'd turn it on

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:45.160
as a reward after doing an 
hour of homework, right?

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:00.780
This is impossible!

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:03.220
My sweat's dripping onto my notebook!

00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:06.640
I'm forcing myself to wait for my 
ice cream reward too, you know!

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:10.780
A phone call?

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:12.440
Who is it?

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:13.690
It's a text message...

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:20.720
So hot...

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:22.310
Sh-Shinobu.

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:25.570
Can you fillet a fish?

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:26.300
Huh?

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:28.250
No, of course not.

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:32.120
Inbox
From: Inuzuka-sensei
Sub: Sorry for the sudden message

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:29.560
Why?

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.120
Well...

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:35.040
Hello.

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:39.580
I brought these to share.

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:42.760
The eyes are so pretty!

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:45.900
Those look delicious!

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:46.640
That was fast!

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:49.440
But are you sure we can have them?

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:50.400
Yes.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:53.770
The two of us went to the sea today,

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:58.580
but it was so hot, we decided 
to come straight back home.

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:01.530
On our way back,

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:05.030
we happened to see a family 
from the neighborhood fishing.

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:10.730
They saw how interested 
Tsumugi was in the fish,

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:14.520
and they ended up giving us some.

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:16.460
Right, Tsumugi?

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.170
Uh-huh...

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:24.490
What's wrong, Tsumugi-chan?

00:05:24.980 --> 00:05:26.330
You seem down.

00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:33.430
I said I wanted to show them to you.

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:37.100
Daddy said it might be a bother.

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:40.650
N-No... I meant if we just 
came over without warning.

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:44.010
Not at all!

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:47.030
If you wanted to show me,

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:49.020
that makes me really happy.

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:52.270
Huh?

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:56.960
What's gotten into her?

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:58.900
Did something happen?

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:00.330
Well, you see...

00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:02.500
I bet she's hot!

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:05.310
Should we turn up the air conditioner?

00:06:05.310 --> 00:06:07.630
No, no. No need.

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:12.220
She's just being a bit of a baby lately.

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:14.350
I'm not a baby.

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:16.090
I'm a kitty.

00:06:16.090 --> 00:06:18.390
I'm a kitty, so it's okay.

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:19.850
I see.

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:21.990
A kitty?

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:25.820
Meow-what?

00:06:26.310 --> 00:06:29.290
Meow! Meow! Meow! Meow!

00:06:29.290 --> 00:06:30.940
Meow! Meow!

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:33.930
They're having a conversation...

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:36.170
Shinobu has a big family,

00:06:36.170 --> 00:06:38.140
so she's used to dealing with little kids.

00:06:40.590 --> 00:06:44.270
Sorry for coming over without 
making arrangements first.

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:47.320
No, no. I like aji.

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:48.590
And...

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:51.710
I don't know exactly what's going on,

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:55.050
but if coming here makes 
Tsumugi-chan feel better,

00:06:55.050 --> 00:06:56.850
that makes me happy.

00:06:57.590 --> 00:06:59.000
Thank you.

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:03.230
Anyway, about the fish...

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:03.860
Yes?

00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:08.350
I contacted my mother, and she said 
she won't be back until tonight.

00:07:08.350 --> 00:07:10.440
We might have to put them in the freezer.

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:12.570
I'm sorry.

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:17.080
I thought Yagi could do it, so I called him...

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:18.330
Fish?

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:21.540
I've actually got lunch customers 
here for once, so no.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:23.980
<i>I'll show you some other time.</i>

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:28.880
You should just fillet them yourself!

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:31.480
I couldn't...

00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:33.590
I've never done it before.

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:35.970
And I don't know how.

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:37.720
Well, I mean...

00:07:38.030 --> 00:07:41.120
I just looked it up after Kotori asked.

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:43.540
And nowadays... Look.

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:47.940
<b>The Simple Way to Fillet A Fish</b>

00:07:44.510 --> 00:07:47.940
These days, there are all 
kinds of videos like this.

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:50.080
This is your chance to practice!

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:53.200
No, I just brought them over to share.

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:56.890
I don't know if I should use the 
kitchen without permission.

00:07:56.890 --> 00:07:59.700
Um, actually, I got permission

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.040
for you to cook here if you want to.

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:05.560
Then it's decided!

00:08:06.640 --> 00:08:08.000
Come on!

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:10.410
I've never done it either, but I'll help.

00:08:10.410 --> 00:08:11.590
No...

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:12.720
What?

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:16.640
We're all going to eat the fish together?

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:21.930
Sensei, isn't this the time 
for you to try your best?

00:08:27.410 --> 00:08:28.360
You're right!

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:29.630
Fish...

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:31.660
Is it okay?

00:08:32.210 --> 00:08:33.320
Can you do it?

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:34.280
I ca—

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:35.030
I will!

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:41.380
Daddy will do his best,

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:42.420
so just wait, okay?

00:08:43.220 --> 00:08:44.160
Okay...

00:08:45.990 --> 00:08:47.670
So, what should we make?

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:49.310
Aji, huh?

00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:51.390
Aji are good for...

00:08:51.390 --> 00:08:54.330
Since they're fresh, maybe sashimi?

00:08:54.330 --> 00:08:55.930
Or tataki, since they're aji?

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:57.920
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:08:57.920 --> 00:09:01.130
Tsumugi doesn't eat that much raw fish.

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:04.880
She doesn't eat sushi?

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:06.190
She does, but...

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:09.440
My favorite sushi is egg.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:11.130
I see...

00:09:12.390 --> 00:09:14.120
Egg sushi is good.

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:17.410
Then we should cook them, right?

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:20.480
What are some things we could make

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:21.910
Aji Recipes

00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:23.720
with what we have on hand 
that Tsumugi would like?

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:25.410
Everyone Recommends: 404 Aji Recipes [easy cooking] Simple and delicious...
Fish cooking 37 Aji Recipes [easy cooking] Simple and delicious recipes...
Aji Recipes How To Make [Simple Popularity Ranking] | Farm Recipes...

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:31.960
But since they're fresh, 
I'd really love to eat them raw...

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:34.780
The grown-ups can try a little to taste them.

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:38.430
<b>Aji Namerou</b>

00:09:35.480 --> 00:09:38.430
We can turn them into namerou 
and have them with rice,

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:42.140
then cook them and turn them into sangayaki!

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:44.290
How about that?

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:45.640
Sangayaki?

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:48.500
It's like a fish Hamburg steak!

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:50.400
Hamburg steak...

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:53.400
I love Hamburg steak.

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:55.320
Then it's settled!

00:09:56.300 --> 00:09:56.990
All right.

00:09:56.990 --> 00:10:00.410
We'll start by taking the aji
we just washed, and filleting it.

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:03.930
First we take off the scales on 
both sides that are called "zeigo."

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:06.160
The zeigo?

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:08.040
Look.

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:10.710
Okay.

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:12.590
Here?

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:13.900
Here, right?

00:10:13.900 --> 00:10:14.440
Yeah.

00:10:14.440 --> 00:10:16.970
The knife should just slide in right there.

00:10:17.480 --> 00:10:19.100
You're really good!

00:10:19.100 --> 00:10:20.300
Both sides, okay?

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:21.160
Okay.

00:10:23.610 --> 00:10:26.000
Now we take off the rest of the scales.

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:27.950
Hold the knife upside-down.

00:10:27.950 --> 00:10:28.680
Okay.

00:10:31.290 --> 00:10:33.480
Rinse the scales off with water...

00:10:34.140 --> 00:10:36.440
Then chop off the head.

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:40.410
Put the knife in diagonally 
under the pectoral fin,

00:10:40.810 --> 00:10:43.670
then cut in hard, once on each side.

00:10:46.050 --> 00:10:47.900
The bone's pretty hard, huh?

00:10:48.310 --> 00:10:52.040
That's why we use a strong, 
heavy deba knife, I bet.

00:10:58.450 --> 00:11:00.570
So cruel!

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:09.310
Okay.

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:10.760
Let's move on to the next step.

00:11:10.760 --> 00:11:13.020
Next is the internal organs.

00:11:15.170 --> 00:11:18.260
You don't want to get food poisoning, 
so make sure you get them all out.

00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:20.030
Okay.

00:11:23.080 --> 00:11:27.940
Um... Cut into the stomach from the head end,

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:29.880
and up to the anal fin...

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:36.290
Gruesome...

00:11:36.290 --> 00:11:37.830
Is it okay?

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:40.260
Is it okay for her to see this?

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:42.970
I'm gonna see!

00:11:43.340 --> 00:11:44.440
What?

00:11:44.440 --> 00:11:46.300
Are you okay, Tsumugi?

00:11:46.310 --> 00:11:47.760
Aren't you scared?

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:48.870
I'm fine!

00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:50.140
'Cause I'm a kitty now!

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:52.890
Y-Yeah?

00:11:52.890 --> 00:11:55.630
There's an awful lot of blood...

00:11:55.630 --> 00:11:58.780
Now let's take off the chiai along the backbone.

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:00.150
The chiai?

00:12:00.150 --> 00:12:03.320
The red part right next to the backbone.

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:05.040
You cut into it a little,

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:07.450
and then kind of just scratch it off.

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:10.680
Use the end of the knife.

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:11.660
Okay!

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:13.920
Right, right! You're doing great!

00:12:15.230 --> 00:12:16.700
It's okay.

00:12:16.700 --> 00:12:18.800
Daddy's not scared.

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:21.360
Hold it under running water

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:24.140
as you use your nails to scratch out what's left.

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:27.150
The blood is what makes it smell,

00:12:27.150 --> 00:12:28.670
so make sure you get it all out.

00:12:28.670 --> 00:12:32.070
Carefully fold it up in a paper towel...

00:12:34.090 --> 00:12:36.590
Get all the water out, 
both inside and outside.

00:12:36.590 --> 00:12:37.560
Oh, okay.

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:44.610
Good! All set!

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:48.580
It's kind of a relief to make it this far, huh?

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:50.960
This is exhausting...

00:12:52.550 --> 00:12:55.790
I bet you're just getting nervous, 
and it's tiring you out.

00:12:56.280 --> 00:12:57.290
You've got that right.

00:12:57.290 --> 00:12:58.940
You have to relax!

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:03.220
Oh, but it's going okay so far.

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:05.880
This is where it gets hard!

00:13:13.430 --> 00:13:18.190
Filleting Fish

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:18.190
Now it's time to fillet it!

00:13:18.190 --> 00:13:19.680
Here, here!

00:13:19.680 --> 00:13:21.530
This is what we're going for!

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:25.120
Okay.

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:26.010
Here I go.

00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:27.410
Put the knife into the stomach.

00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:32.290
The end of the knife will hit the 
backbone, so follow along that.

00:13:33.140 --> 00:13:34.150
Huh?

00:13:34.630 --> 00:13:36.000
It's not moving.

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:37.400
Let me see...

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:39.790
Oh, Sensei,

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:42.840
you have to hold the knife 
like this, toward the fish...

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:43.760
Diagonally!

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:45.580
Try putting it in diagonally.

00:13:47.570 --> 00:13:48.930
You're right!

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:50.750
It's easier to cut!

00:13:50.750 --> 00:13:52.250
Now the back.

00:13:58.080 --> 00:14:00.080
It's in two pieces now!

00:14:01.280 --> 00:14:02.770
Are you okay?

00:14:02.770 --> 00:14:03.880
Want me to take over?

00:14:04.340 --> 00:14:06.300
It's not making you sick?

00:14:06.300 --> 00:14:08.660
No, I'm fine.

00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:11.050
Since I've come this far,

00:14:11.050 --> 00:14:13.830
I want to learn how to do it before I go.

00:14:23.350 --> 00:14:24.880
I did it!

00:14:26.480 --> 00:14:28.130
It's filleted!

00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:30.180
Good work!

00:14:31.090 --> 00:14:33.560
That took, like, twenty minutes!

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:35.160
Look, look!

00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:37.060
Isn't Daddy amazing?

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:38.790
He worked really hard!

00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:40.810
Yeah!

00:14:41.120 --> 00:14:45.280
The middle part ended up 
looking the tastiest, though.

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:47.150
Don't worry, don't worry.

00:14:47.150 --> 00:14:48.620
You'll get used to it.

00:14:49.540 --> 00:14:53.370
Um, before we cut up the next aji...

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:57.020
Want to try a bite?

00:14:57.450 --> 00:14:59.660
Yeah! Good idea!

00:14:59.660 --> 00:15:02.730
Just cut off a few tiny slices...

00:15:04.640 --> 00:15:06.200
Grate some ginger...

00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:07.550
Soy sauce! Soy sauce!

00:15:11.960 --> 00:15:12.950
Here I go.

00:15:13.770 --> 00:15:16.070
M-May I try some, too?

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:19.600
This is great!

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:21.260
It's so tender!

00:15:21.260 --> 00:15:22.590
It's good!

00:15:22.590 --> 00:15:24.480
It's very fresh!

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:27.360
I... I want some, too!

00:15:28.560 --> 00:15:29.790
Are you sure?

00:15:29.790 --> 00:15:30.870
I want some!

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:34.650
Maybe this small one, then...

00:15:36.880 --> 00:15:38.660
No ginger, okay?

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:49.380
I ate it!

00:15:49.640 --> 00:15:53.830
Daddy! Keep going, keep going!
Do the next fish!

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:57.780
Why are you so excited all of a sudden?

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:00.350
That...

00:16:02.260 --> 00:16:03.730
turned in to this...

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:06.560
and ended up here!

00:16:06.560 --> 00:16:09.110
Isn't that amazing?

00:16:09.520 --> 00:16:10.600
Know what I mean?

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:18.820
It's scary and fun and amazing!

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:25.040
Yeah... You're right.

00:16:29.220 --> 00:16:31.290
When you were born,

00:16:31.290 --> 00:16:33.450
you were really little.

00:16:34.420 --> 00:16:37.780
I was so worried and nervous,

00:16:37.780 --> 00:16:40.470
but Mommy laughed and said it was okay.

00:16:43.120 --> 00:16:47.100
You've been eating all your 
fish and meat and vegetables,

00:16:47.560 --> 00:16:49.850
and growing up into a big girl.

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:56.530
It really is amazing!

00:16:57.380 --> 00:16:58.450
Yeah!

00:16:58.730 --> 00:17:00.380
Wow, Tsumugi-chan!

00:17:00.380 --> 00:17:01.480
That is amazing!

00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:04.040
Wow, big girl Tsumugi!

00:17:04.040 --> 00:17:06.410
I'm kind of excited!

00:17:06.410 --> 00:17:10.170
Tsumugi, I'll make you another 
yummy meal today, okay?

00:17:10.170 --> 00:17:14.820
Yeah! And I'll eat a whole lot today, okay?

00:17:16.560 --> 00:17:18.810
You mean like you always do?

00:17:23.070 --> 00:17:26.080
Okay, let's go on to the next one!

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:27.000
Right!

00:17:28.100 --> 00:17:31.760
Wow, you're getting used to it already.

00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:34.010
It's easier than the first one.

00:17:34.470 --> 00:17:37.340
I'll dance, so do your best!

00:17:37.340 --> 00:17:39.120
Okay!

00:17:41.440 --> 00:17:44.650
Ready go, ready go, fishy-fish!

00:17:44.650 --> 00:17:48.120
Ready go, ready go, ready go!

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:51.320
Fish! Fish! Fishy-fish!

00:17:55.660 --> 00:17:57.050
To make namerou,

00:17:57.050 --> 00:18:01.670
cut the aji meat into small
pieces without crushing it.

00:18:01.670 --> 00:18:02.510
Okay.

00:18:02.510 --> 00:18:06.650
We mince the ginger and cut 
the green onion into tiny slices.

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:08.600
Leave that to me!

00:18:11.680 --> 00:18:15.320
For two aji, we'd want about 
a tablespoon of miso, I think.

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:19.720
Hey, hey, can I use the heads 
to make miso soup?

00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:22.950
Looking at them made me want to make some.

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:25.760
Wow, you can do that?

00:18:25.760 --> 00:18:26.920
Go ahead!

00:18:26.920 --> 00:18:28.080
Okay!

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:31.530
Ish-ish fishy-fish! Ish-ish fishy-fish!

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:35.370
What goes in the soup... 
Daikon and mitsuba, I guess.

00:18:36.130 --> 00:18:37.980
Is this about right?

00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:39.090
Yup.

00:18:39.090 --> 00:18:43.220
Now form it into little balls and flatten them,

00:18:43.220 --> 00:18:45.110
then fry them in a frying pan.

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:49.850
Ish-ish-ish!

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:53.160
These will be the sangayaki.

00:18:54.670 --> 00:18:58.070
Wow, it smells so good!

00:18:58.390 --> 00:19:00.250
It's almost done.

00:19:00.250 --> 00:19:01.180
Just wait.

00:19:01.180 --> 00:19:02.320
Okay!

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:05.080
Let me in.

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:06.080
Yagi!

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:08.040
Come on in!

00:19:08.470 --> 00:19:12.300
Too bad! You're late, and late 
people don't get any food!

00:19:12.300 --> 00:19:16.200
What? But you've still got one left.

00:19:21.240 --> 00:19:22.800
I-It's done!

00:19:23.830 --> 00:19:25.930
The namerou and sangayaki...

00:19:26.660 --> 00:19:28.310
are ready!

00:19:29.620 --> 00:19:31.060
Fish head miso soup

00:19:31.390 --> 00:19:33.560
and piping hot rice, too!

00:19:33.560 --> 00:19:35.820
What a feast!

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:38.030
Let's eat!

00:19:45.590 --> 00:19:47.370
Yum!

00:19:49.480 --> 00:19:50.830
It's so good!

00:19:51.140 --> 00:19:53.050
I'll have the namerou.

00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:58.570
It has such a nice Japanese miso flavor...

00:19:58.570 --> 00:20:01.420
And you can really taste 
the fat from the aji.

00:20:01.420 --> 00:20:03.230
You're right, it's good!

00:20:03.230 --> 00:20:05.180
It goes great with the rice!

00:20:05.180 --> 00:20:06.760
This is good miso.

00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:08.550
It's so good!

00:20:08.550 --> 00:20:10.220
Daddy! Daddy!

00:20:11.090 --> 00:20:11.980
What is it?

00:20:12.710 --> 00:20:14.430
Today was amazing!

00:20:14.430 --> 00:20:16.650
The sea, and the fishies!

00:20:16.980 --> 00:20:19.150
It was all so fun!

00:20:21.880 --> 00:20:23.150
You're right.

00:20:24.130 --> 00:20:25.660
It was fun.

00:22:10.640 --> 00:22:14.360
Namerou tastes great if 
you wrap it in seaweed.

00:22:16.610 --> 00:22:18.770
What's this? What's this?

00:22:18.770 --> 00:22:20.200
Fish bone senbei.

00:22:21.400 --> 00:22:22.730
It looks good!

00:22:23.120 --> 00:22:24.910
Nice, Yagi-chin!

00:22:24.910 --> 00:22:27.740
"Chin"? I'm older than you, you know.

00:22:29.780 --> 00:22:31.000
Crunchy!

00:22:31.000 --> 00:22:32.140
Yum!

00:22:32.140 --> 00:22:35.850
Actually, when I went to 
pick up Tsumugi earlier,

00:22:35.850 --> 00:22:37.500
I smelled something sweet.

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:39.480
Were you making something?

00:22:40.440 --> 00:22:41.290
Yeah.

00:22:41.730 --> 00:22:44.600
I made a cake for a customer's birthday.

00:22:46.030 --> 00:22:48.220
You don't look like a cake maker.

00:22:48.500 --> 00:22:50.840
Does it matter what I look like?

00:22:50.840 --> 00:22:54.260
I'm so jealous that you can make sweets!

00:22:54.770 --> 00:22:56.470
When did you learn?

00:22:57.770 --> 00:23:01.520
Come to think of it, when we were in school,

00:23:01.520 --> 00:23:05.220
you once asked me what kind of sweets I liked.

00:23:06.390 --> 00:23:08.190
Yagi-chan, that's yucky!

00:23:08.190 --> 00:23:10.090
What are you doing?

00:23:10.090 --> 00:23:11.360
S-Sorry...

00:23:11.640 --> 00:23:16.280
You were using Sensei to 
help you learn to cook, huh?

00:23:16.280 --> 00:23:17.990
I... I guess.

00:23:19.380 --> 00:23:21.300
You're really dedicated, huh?

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:25.580
Huh?

00:23:26.020 --> 00:23:27.850
All the fish bone senbei's gone!

00:23:28.480 --> 00:23:29.850
When did that happen?

00:23:29.850 --> 00:23:32.970
Ts-Tsumugi, you're eating too much!

00:23:33.290 --> 00:23:35.340
Thank you for the food!
